425	  /**
426	   * Pre-fills the {@link BitmapPool} using the given sizes.
427	   *
428	   * <p>Enough Bitmaps are added to completely fill the pool, so most or all of the Bitmaps
429	   * currently in the pool will be evicted. Bitmaps are allocated according to the weights of the
430	   * given sizes, where each size gets (weight / prefillWeightSum) percent of the pool to fill.
431	   *
432	   * <p>Note - Pre-filling is done asynchronously using and {@link IdleHandler}. Any currently
433	   * running pre-fill will be cancelled and replaced by a call to this method.
434	   *
435	   * <p>This method should be used with caution, overly aggressive pre-filling is substantially
436	   * worse than not pre-filling at all. Pre-filling should only be started in onCreate to avoid
437	   * constantly clearing and re-filling the {@link BitmapPool}. Rotation should be carefully
438	   * considered as well. It may be worth calling this method only when no saved instance state
439	   * exists so that pre-filling only happens when the Activity is first created, rather than on
440	   * every rotation.
