210	   * each other. As a rule, Glide does not add {@link RequestListener}s to thumbnail requests
211	   * automatically. That means that {@link RequestListener}s track the state of exactly one request
212	   * in the chain. For example, if you start a primary request with a single nested thumbnail and
213	   * you add a {@link RequestListener} only to the primary request, then the {@link RequestListener}
214	   * will only be notified when the primary request succeeds or fails. If the thumbnail succeeds,
215	   * but the primary request fails, the {@link RequestListener} added to the primary request will
216	   * still be called with {@link RequestListener#onLoadFailed(GlideException, Object, Target,
217	   * boolean)}. In the same scenario, the {@link RequestListener} added only to the primary request
218	   * will not have {@link RequestListener#onResourceReady(Object, Object, Target, DataSource,
219	   * boolean)} called when the thumbnail request finishes successfully. Similarly, if you add a
220	   * {@link RequestListener} only to a thumbnail request, but not the primary request, that {@code
221	   * listener} will only be called for changes related to the thumbnail request. If the thumbnail
222	   * request fails, the {@code listener} added to the thumbnail request will be immediately called
223	   * via {@link RequestListener#onLoadFailed(GlideException, Object, Target, boolean)}, even though
224	   * the primary request may eventually succeed. It is perfectly possible to add a {@link
225	   * RequestListener} to both the primary and a thumbnail request. If you do so, the {@link
226	   * RequestListener} will be called independently for each request when it finishes. Keep in mind
227	   * that if any parent request finishes before its thumbnail request(s), it will attempt to cancel
228	   * those requests. As a result there's no guarantee that a {@link RequestListener} added to a
229	   * thumbnail request will actually be called with either success or failure. These same patterns
230	   * hold for arbitrarily nested thumbnails. The {@code listener} is only called for the requests it
231	   * is added to and may not be called for every thumbnail request if those requests are cancelled
232	   * due to the completion of a parent request.
