198	   * in the correct order. The system calls required to register/unregister the receiver and to
199	   * determine connectivity status are expensive to run on the main thread. isConnected and
200	   * isRegistered should only be used on the serial background thread. Listeners should only be
201	   * notified on the main thread. Because of the delays caused by punting threads, listeners may be
202	   * notified with the incorrect state. Howeve the strict ordering means that they will shortly
203	   * after be notified with the correct state.
